Third-party software this code uses (installed separately, not included in this repository):

- basic_agent (MIT) — agent loop for the local-model chat session. https://github.com/Taeksu-Kim/basic_agent
- FastAPI, Starlette, Uvicorn, Pydantic (MIT / BSD) — the local server.
- Playwright for Python (Apache-2.0) — end-to-end checks and the "playwright" script export format.
- faster-whisper (MIT), CTranslate2 (MIT) — optional Whisper speech-to-text server (tools/stt_server.py).
  Whisper model weights (MIT) are downloaded by faster-whisper.
- Supertonic (see its own license) — optional, only for generating test speech in tools/voice_check.py.
- numpy (BSD-3-Clause) — optional, speech tools.

Services used at run time, chosen by the user:
- A local OpenAI-compatible LLM server (e.g. vLLM). Model weights are under their own licenses.
- Claude Code (optional chat session) — page content is sent to Anthropic when this session is chosen.
- Google speech recognition through Chrome's built-in Web Speech API (optional voice engine) — the user's voice is sent to Google.

